{"t": 1794106763.8493938, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "\u26a0\ufe0f This change introduced a production reconciliation bug.\n\nCommit 8c2f1d0 replaced `round(amount_minor * rate)` with `int(amount_minor * rate)` in `worker/rates.py`. `int()` truncates toward zero instead of rounding to the nearest minor unit, so fractional conversions lose 1 minor unit (e.g. expected 1100, got 1099) and ledger reconciliation fails.\n\nSentry error: https://acme.sentry.io/issues/LEDGER-WORKER-9A/ (LEDGER-WORKER-9A \u2014 ReconciliationMismatch: converted totals off by 1 minor unit, first seen in ledger-worker@2026.11.3, 2,201 events).\n\nFix: restored rounding in `worker/rates.py` (`return round(amount_minor * rate)`).", "issue_number": 412, "owner": "acme", "repo": "ledger-worker"}, "ok": true}
